      "path": ".agdf/control/runs/run-d2818184-27fc-40ae-9195-70d080d3e926/documents/TP.md",
      "digest": "sha256:c3821a2e9247a82141accf097456cb75a526fe5b3f217c6a814815932f9e3fbf",
      "statement": "| AC-005 | SDD-007 | T-010 | SCN-011 | With an injected clock a new journal line for the current root triggers a run-view call and a notice within one 2-second tick; lines of other roots are ignored with win32 separator and case normalization; malformed lines are skipped; without fingerprint change, event or language change no run-view call happens | `claude-companion-adapter-test.js` output with process-call counts |",
      "intended_change": "| AC-005 | SDD-007 | T-010 | SCN-011 | With an injected clock a new journal line for the current root triggers a run-view call and a notice within one 2-second tick; lines of other roots are ignored with win32 separator and case normalization; malformed lines are skipped; without fingerprint change, event or language change no run-view call happens | `claude-companion-adapter-test.js` output with process-call counts |\n| AC-005 | SDD-007 | T-015 | SCN-024 | An event of the shown run renders without a run name, an event of another run with its objective or, without objective, its short id `run-xxxxxxxx`; notice toasts carry no run id; the de and en catalogs carry `events.ofRun` | `claude-companion-test.js` text cases and `claude-companion-adapter-test.js` toast cases |",
      "reason": "Owner request of 2026-11-06 during the native check (finding F5): event lines and toasts repeated the full run id the header already shows; the change exists in the code but no TP task or scenario covers it."
    },
    {
      "type": "TP",
      "path": ".agdf/control/runs/run-d2818184-27fc-40ae-9195-70d080d3e926/documents/TP.md",
      "digest": "sha256:c3821a2e9247a82141accf097456cb75a526fe5b3f217c6a814815932f9e3fbf",
      "statement": "| AC-009 | SDD-010 | T-006 | SCN-016 | The companion imports no Core module; its only process call is the read-only `run-view` command; it writes only `companion-state.json`; its hooks never block or change an MCP call; the digest of `.agdf/control` is unchanged across simulated companion activity and real run-view calls; an injected control write or a second command in a probe module makes the check fail | `claude-companion-integrity-test.js` output |",
      "intended_change": "| AC-009 | SDD-010 | T-006 | SCN-016 | The companion imports no Core module; its only process call is the read-only `run-view` command; it writes only `companion-state.json`; its hooks never block or change an MCP call; the digest of `.agdf/control` is unchanged across simulated companion activity and real run-view calls; an injected control write or a second command in a probe module makes the check fail | `claude-companion-integrity-test.js` output |\n| AC-009 | SDD-010 | T-014 | SCN-023 | Every companion module uses `$` nouns only at their call site, `register.mjs` holds exactly one `$.process.run(` wrapper and `run-state.mjs` the single `processes.run(` call; the check fails against the code that passed `$.process` as a value; `claude plugin validate` reports no error for the generated plugin | `claude-companion-adapter-test.js` and `claude-companion-integrity-test.js` output, red run against the old code, `claude plugin validate` output |",
      "reason": "Native check T-013 finding F1 (evidence/T-013-NATIVE_CHECK-01.md): the desktop host refused the whole companion hooks module because register.mjs passed $.process as a value; the fix exists in the code since 2026-11-06 but no TP task or scenario covers it."
    },
